From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Pace the main loop to the render thread; spin-free
 frame cap

The main thread publishes a frame per pass into a two-slot mailbox that
keeps only the latest frame. When the render side is the bottleneck (about
80 FPS in busy scenes) half the passes build a frame, with its 4 MB copy,
that is overwritten without being drawn.

- At the start of each main loop pass, wait for the render thread to take
  the frame published last (state[wr % n] != 0 at 8294CA9C, read from
  guest memory), woken by a hook on the take's return (821A866C). The wait
  times out after twice the longest of the last 8 render times plus 4 ms
  (10-64 ms); after 2 timeouts with no take in between, pacing stops until
  the render thread takes a frame again. Pacing stops while the render
  thread needs more than 30 ms per frame and resumes below 24 ms, where
  waiting would cost more latency than it saves.
- Late start (on by default): after that wait, sleep so the next frame is
  ready a margin (1 ms and up, raised by 1 ms whenever the render thread
  had to wait for a late-started frame) before the render thread finishes
  the current one, using the shortest recent render time and the longest
  recent main pass. This keeps the input latency of building frames
  continuously.
- The frame cap sleeps until each deadline on host ticks, with a
  high-resolution waitable timer on Windows (NanoSleep elsewhere or if
  unavailable), instead of yielding in a loop for the last millisecond
  while taking the guest clock lock. halo3_pacer_spin_us adds an optional
  busy-wait tail.
- halo3_render_thread_sleep (on by default): the render thread waits up to
  1 ms for a publish (821A85D0, woken from 820802CC) instead of polling,
  and sleeps 1 ms per spin while the main thread draws (821A8730, mode 0).
- Stats: frames taken and overwritten untaken, render drawing and waiting
  time per frame, main thread time per frame, waits, timeouts, unpaced
  passes, late starts and margin, and the cap's sleep, spin and lateness;
  the GPU command processor thread's time split and counts (the GPU
  thread timing counters).

Cvars: halo3_pace_to_render, halo3_pace_late_start, halo3_pacer_spin_us,
halo3_render_thread_sleep.
