 // To unlock the frame rate we skip the three vblank waits, publish a frame on
 // every pass, and feed main_time_update's result from the host clock instead
 // of the vblank counter, so dt stays exact at any frame rate and the
-// simulation speed is unchanged. The frame-rate cap is a host-side wait at the
-// start of the main loop body, before input is read; the render thread draws
-// as fast as frames are published. Presents outside the main loop (loading
+// simulation speed is unchanged. Presents outside the main loop (loading
 // screens drawn while the main thread loads) are already spaced out by the
 // code that triggers them. Everything is decided per frame from cvars,
 // because the per-game config is only loaded after the title module (and
 // these hooks) are set up.
+//
+// The frame queue (8294CA9C) is a two-slot mailbox. The main thread publishes
+// into slot wr % n (sub_821D5888): a 4 MB copy, then state = 1, overwriting a
+// frame nobody took. The render thread polls slot rd % n; its take
+// (sub_821D5A08) sets the state to 0 and then wr++, and it draws while
+// holding that slot, which its release (sub_821D5B30) frees with rd++. So
+// "the frame published last hasn't been taken" is exactly state[wr % n] != 0,
+// and while the main thread doesn't publish only the render thread changes
+// it, from 1 to 0.
+//
+// Pacing, all at the start of the main loop body, before input is read:
+// - Wait for the render thread to take the frame published last, so the main
+//   thread doesn't build frames that are overwritten without being drawn
+//   (about 40% of passes when the render side is the bottleneck). Skipped
+//   when the render thread draws too slowly for it to pay off, and bounded by
+//   a timeout in case the render thread stalls.
+// - Late start: after that wait, sleep so the next frame is ready just before
+//   the render thread finishes the current one, which keeps the input latency
+//   of building frames continuously.
+// - The frame-rate cap, sleeping until each frame's deadline.
+// The render thread itself busy-polls for frames, and spins while the main
+// thread draws (mode 0); it sleeps in both instead.
 
